PUBLIC RESPONSE: {E}

The accredited investor (AI) definition is set out in NI 45-106 (Ontario). Relevant categories include:
- an individual whose income exceeds $200 k ($300 k combined with spouse) in each of the two preceding years and who reasonably expects to exceed the threshold in the current year;
- an individual (alone or with spouse) whose net financial assets exceed $1 M ($5 M combined) or whose net assets exceed $5 M;
- any entity (corporation, limited partnership, etc.) whose most recent financial statements show net assets of at least $5 M; and
- any entity all of whose security-holders or partners are themselves AIs.

A, B, C and D each satisfy at least one of the above tests on the facts given. E does not: neither Alex nor Bob meets any individual-income or asset test, so the “all owners are AIs” route is unavailable; the corporation’s balance sheet shows only $5.2 M of net assets once the stated liabilities are deducted, and the value of the investment properties is not supplied, so the “net assets ≥ $5 M” route is also unavailable. Therefore E is not an AI.}

